        "title": "Chemosynthesis and Alternative Energy Pathways",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "For ~3.8 billion years of Earth's history, biology assumed sunlight was the non-negotiable\nenergy source. The 1977 discovery of hydrothermal vents and their dense, thriving\ncommunities shattered that assumption. Chemosynthesis — primary production using chemical\noxidation reactions rather than photosynthesis — provides the energy base for entire\necosystems in permanent darkness."
